<h1>How to Play Mark Six</h1>
<p class="lead">Mark Six is the Hong Kong Jockey Club lottery. Here is the idea in plain words.</p>
<h2>The basics</h2>
<ol>
  <li>A player chooses 6 different numbers from 1 to 49.</li>
  <li>In each draw, 6 winning numbers and 1 extra number are drawn.</li>
  <li>Prizes depend on how many of your numbers match.</li>
</ol>
<h2>The 7 prize divisions</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Division</th><th>What you need to match</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>1st</td><td>All 6 winning numbers</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2nd</td><td>5 winning numbers + the extra number</td></tr>
    <tr><td>3rd</td><td>5 winning numbers</td></tr>
    <tr><td>4th</td><td>4 winning numbers + the extra number</td></tr>
    <tr><td>5th</td><td>4 winning numbers</td></tr>
    <tr><td>6th</td><td>3 winning numbers + the extra number</td></tr>
    <tr><td>7th</td><td>3 winning numbers</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<h2>Where to play</h2>
<p>Only the Hong Kong Jockey Club can accept Mark Six bets, and only where the law allows it. This site does not sell tickets or take bets. We publish results, prizes and tools to help you understand the game. Check the official HKJC rules for prices, draw days and claim deadlines.</p>
<p><a class="btn" href="/pick">Try the number generator</a></p>
